<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <AssemblyName>ADO.Query.Core</AssemblyName>
    <PackageId>NET.Database.QueryLayer</PackageId>
    <GenerateAssemblyConfigurationAttribute>false</GenerateAssemblyConfigurationAttribute>
    <GenerateAssemblyCompanyAttribute>false</GenerateAssemblyCompanyAttribute>
    <GenerateAssemblyProductAttribute>false</GenerateAssemblyProductAttribute>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;netstandard2.1;net47;net48;net6.0;net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <Version>3.0.0</Version>
    <Authors>Omar del Valle Rodriguez</Authors>
    <Description>NET-Database query layer components will be a useful addition to any application or website to create SQL queries to your database in a OO way. It supports the majority of different database types such as SQL Server® MySQL® o PostgreSQL®, but is easy extend to any ADO.NET provider.</Description>
    <Copyright>2016</Copyright>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/iTravelMix/NET-Database-query-layer</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/iTravelMix/NET-Database-query-layer</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>- Update Slapper.AutoMapper to 3.0.0
- Breaking: Slapper 3.0.0 scopes instance caches to each mapping call, eliminating cross-query instance reuse and cache collisions. The default QueryMapper no longer shares or merges instances across queries, even for the same destination type and Id; keepCache and RemoveCacheAfterExecuteQuery no longer control cross-query instance reuse.
- Multi-target: netstandard2.0, netstandard2.1, net47, net48, net6.0, net8.0, net9.0, net10.0</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <AssemblyVersion>3.0.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CSharp" Version="4.7.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Npgsql" Version="4.1.13" />
    <PackageReference Include="Slapper.AutoMapper" Version="3.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Collections.NonGeneric" Version="4.3.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Data.Common" Version="4.3.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Data.SqlClient" Version="4.8.6" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Dynamic.Runtime" Version="4.3.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
